# REPLACE the placeholder fields before publishing, and add the Zenodo DOI once
# the first release has been archived.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Enhanced Radial Stress Method for the Vierendeel bending design of perforated steel beams with circular or elliptical openings."
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Georgios"
    family-names: "Psyrras"
    email: "giorgos.psyrras@city.ac.uk"
    affiliation: "City St George's, University of London"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PsyrrasG/enhanced-radial-stress-method"
abstract: >-
  Algorithmic implementation of the Enhanced Radial Stress Method for the
  Vierendeel bending design of perforated steel I-beams with circular or elliptical web
  openings, in accordance with BS EN 1993-1-13:2024. Provides four analysis
  modes over a shared vectorised numerical core: the elastic limit of the lower
  and higher moment sides, the plastic capacity with moment redistribution, and
  the state of the opening at a prescribed pair of applied forces.
keywords:
  - structural engineering
  - steel design
  - cellular beams
  - Enhanced RSM
  - Enhanced Radial Stress Method
  - Vierendeel bending
  - Eurocode 3
